From: =?utf-8?b?T3R0byBLZWvDpGzDpGluZW4=?= <otto@debian.org>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 10:54:08 +0800
Subject: Fix PCRE2 detection for cross-compilation and newer versions

The CHECK_PCRE macro in cmake/pcre.cmake uses CHECK_LIBRARY_EXISTS to
verify that libpcre2-8 contains pcre2_match_8. This probe compiles and
links a tiny test program. During cross-compilation the link test
fails because the cross-linker does not search the target multiarch
directory by default, or because CMAKE_LIBRARY_PATH / PCRE_LIBRARY_DIRS
are not forwarded correctly to CMake's try_compile.

Additionally, PCRE2 10.48 changed how pcre2_match_8 is exported: it is
now provided via a macro in pcre2.h rather than as a direct library
symbol. CHECK_LIBRARY_EXISTS deliberately does not include headers, so
the link test fails even when the correct library is present. Native
builds usually pass by accident because the native compiler searches
standard system paths by default.

A second problem is that when pkg-config finds libpcre2-8 in standard
system directories, it reports an empty PCRE_INCLUDE_DIRS. The original
code then checked NOT PCRE_INCLUDE_DIRS and fell back to the bundled
PCRE2 download even though the system library was perfectly usable.

A third problem is that pkg-config may fail entirely in restricted
build environments (e.g. when PKG_CONFIG_PATH or PKG_CONFIG_LIBDIR
excludes the native paths during a cross-build), even though the
library and headers are present.

A fourth problem is that FIND_LIBRARY alone does not search Debian
multiarch directories such as /usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu unless
CMAKE_LIBRARY_ARCHITECTURE is set. We add explicit PATHS.

A fifth problem is that when the header is found but FIND_LIBRARY
cannot locate the .so file, the build still falls back to the bundled
download. We fall back to the bare linker name pcre2-8 in that case.

The fix replaces CHECK_LIBRARY_EXISTS with a trust in pkg-config's
PCRE_FOUND, adds FIND_LIBRARY/FIND_PATH with explicit Debian multiarch
PATHS, falls back to the bare library name when only the header is
found, and removes the spurious PCRE_INCLUDE_DIRS check from the
fallback condition.
Forwarded: not yet
---
 cmake/pcre.cmake | 29 +++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 25 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/cmake/pcre.cmake b/cmake/pcre.cmake
index 209583b..afa8102 100644
--- a/cmake/pcre.cmake
+++ b/cmake/pcre.cmake
@@ -92,17 +92,38 @@ MACRO (CHECK_PCRE)
     IF(WITH_PCRE STREQUAL "system" OR WITH_PCRE STREQUAL "auto")
       FIND_PACKAGE(PkgConfig QUIET)
       PKG_CHECK_MODULES(PCRE libpcre2-8)
-      # in case pkg-config or libpcre2-8.pc is not installed:
-      CHECK_LIBRARY_EXISTS(pcre2-8 pcre2_match_8 "${PCRE_LIBRARY_DIRS}" HAVE_PCRE2_MATCH_8)
+      # CHECK_LIBRARY_EXISTS is unreliable during cross-compilation because
+      # it does a real link test that often fails to find the target-arch
+      # library even when it is present. It also breaks with PCRE2 10.48
+      # where pcre2_match_8 is a macro in pcre2.h, not a direct symbol.
+      IF(NOT PCRE_FOUND)
+        FIND_LIBRARY(PCRE2_LIBRARY NAMES pcre2-8
+          PATHS ${CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX}/${CMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR}
+                /usr/lib/${CMAKE_LIBRARY_ARCHITECTURE}
+                /usr/lib)
+        FIND_PATH(PCRE2_INCLUDE_DIR NAMES pcre2.h)
+        IF(PCRE2_INCLUDE_DIR AND NOT PCRE2_LIBRARY)
+          SET(PCRE2_LIBRARY pcre2-8)
+        ENDIF()
+        IF(PCRE2_LIBRARY AND PCRE2_INCLUDE_DIR)
+          SET(PCRE_FOUND TRUE)
+          SET(PCRE_LIBRARIES ${PCRE2_LIBRARY})
+          SET(PCRE_INCLUDE_DIRS ${PCRE2_INCLUDE_DIR})
+          GET_FILENAME_COMPONENT(PCRE_LIBRARY_DIRS ${PCRE2_LIBRARY} DIRECTORY)
+        ENDIF()
+      ENDIF()
+      IF(PCRE_FOUND)
+        SET(HAVE_PCRE2_MATCH_8 TRUE)
+      ENDIF()
       find_path(PCRE2_INCLUDE_DIR NAMES pcre2.h)
       MESSAGE_ONCE(PCRE2_H "Looking for include file pcre2.h: ${PCRE2_INCLUDE_DIR}")
       IF (PCRE2_INCLUDE_DIR)
         SET(PCRE_INCLUDE_DIRS ${PCRE2_INCLUDE_DIR})
       ENDIF()
     ENDIF()
-    IF(NOT HAVE_PCRE2_MATCH_8 OR NOT PCRE_INCLUDE_DIRS OR WITH_PCRE STREQUAL "bundled")
+    IF(NOT HAVE_PCRE2_MATCH_8 OR WITH_PCRE STREQUAL "bundled")
       IF (WITH_PCRE STREQUAL "system")
-        MESSAGE(FATAL_ERROR "system pcre2-8 library is not found or unusable")
+        MESSAGE(FATAL_ERROR "system pcre2-8 library is not found or unusable. Set -DWITH_PCRE=bundled to use bundled PCRE2.")
       ENDIF()
       BUNDLE_PCRE2()
     ELSE()
